CLAUDE:
Embeddings aren't supported on this server so we'll go with Option A — keyword-based RAG.

This still fully satisfies the RAG requirement since it retrieves relevant knowledge before 
generating an answer, it just uses keyword matching instead of vector similarity.

How the keyword RAG works:
1. Load the finance knowledge text file
2. Chunk it into sections using rag.chunk_text() (which IS supported)
3. For each question, score chunks by counting keyword matches
4. Take the top 3 most relevant chunks
5. Pass them to get_response() as context for the answer

This approach actually has advantages for this use case:
- No dependency on server capabilities
- Transparent and debuggable — you can see exactly why a chunk was retrieved
- Fast — no embedding computation needed
- Domain-specific keywords work well for finance topics

The knowledge base was built with 14 topic sections covering: budgeting basics, coffee and 
snacks, subscriptions, food and groceries, eating out, social spending, invisible spending, 
shopping, savings goals, emergency funds, payday habits, transport, income, and entertainment.
